# The signs of the units: ℃ and ℉ are a unit's name where one goes (`unit ℃`, `: ℃`); a temperature
# does not add up, so the unit is a count of its own name, as `dB` is. In a name, a sign is E001, and
# `%` is no unit's name
book unit_signs v1

unit ℃
unit %

account sensors : ℃ outside
account probes_below_8℃ : ℃ outside
